IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `au-part3-commencement`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 3, the subsections of s 4 that pass 1 left inert (pass 2).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Pass 1 encoded s 4(1), (2), (4), (5) and (7) in au-part3-commencement.l4 and called (3) and (6)
-- extensions that "add neither a condition nor a day". They add a permission each, and each is encoded here on top of the
-- pass-1 rule that says whether s 4 applies.

§ `Part 3: Commencement of Acts (the rest of section 4)`

§§ `Section 4(3): things done to prepare the exercise`

-- src:248 | (3) Anything may be done before the start time for the purpose of enabling the exercise of the power, or of bringing the appointment or instrument into effect, as if the relevant commencement had occurred.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 4(3) (src:248)
GIVEN enacted IS A BOOLEAN
      `confers the power at a start time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act will commence at the start time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act will be amended at the start time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is done for the purpose of enabling the exercise of the power, or of bringing the appointment or instrument into effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`anything may be done before the start time` enacted `confers the power at a start time` `the Act will commence at the start time` `the Act will be amended at the start time` `the thing is done for the purpose of enabling the exercise of the power, or of bringing the appointment or instrument into effect` MEANS
        `section 4 allows the power to be exercised before the start time` enacted `confers the power at a start time` `the Act will commence at the start time` `the Act will be amended at the start time`
    AND `the thing is done for the purpose of enabling the exercise of the power, or of bringing the appointment or instrument into effect`

§§ `Section 4(6): one instrument partly under section 4(2) and partly under an existing power`

-- src:255 | (6) To avoid doubt, a single instrument may be made before the start time partly under subsection (2) and partly under a power already conferred by an Act.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 4(6) (src:255)
GIVEN enacted IS A BOOLEAN
      `confers the power at a start time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act will commence at the start time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act will be amended at the start time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is made before the start time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one part is made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another part is made under a power already conferred by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a single instrument may be made partly under subsection (2) and partly under an existing power` enacted `confers the power at a start time` `the Act will commence at the start time` `the Act will be amended at the start time` `the instrument is made before the start time` `one part is made under subsection (2)` `another part is made under a power already conferred by an Act` MEANS
        `section 4 allows the power to be exercised before the start time` enacted `confers the power at a start time` `the Act will commence at the start time` `the Act will be amended at the start time`
    AND `the instrument is made before the start time`
    AND `one part is made under subsection (2)`
    AND `another part is made under a power already conferred by an Act`
